For integers \(n,m\ge2\) and \(h\in(0,1)\), define the finite-sample Hoeffding certificate interval
\[
\mathcal I_{h,J_{\mu,n},J_{r,n}}
=\left[
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{sp}}_{h,J_{\mu,n},J_{r,n}}
\pm\left\{B_X(h,J_{\mu,n},J_{r,n})+R_S(h,J_{\mu,n},J_{r,n})+R_T(m)\right\}
\right].
\]
Every term is an explicit function of the observed data and the fixed class constants. The interval has no studentization or zero-standard-error branch.

